  68: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  69:     """
  70:     Extend diagonal rays outward from outer-border segments adjacent to diamond shapes on a checkerboard.
  71: 
  72:     Input structure:
  73:     - Checkerboard bg (two most common colors).
  74:     - Hollow diamond outlines (8-pixel) in a non-bg color (inner border).
  75:     - Short diagonal line segments in another non-bg color adjacent to each diamond edge (outer border).
  76: 
  77:     Rule:
  78:     - For each outer-border segment, determine the outward direction (perpendicular to the segment, away from the diamond).
  79:     - From each endpoint of the segment, cast a diagonal ray outward, painting over bg pixels with the segment's color until hitting a non-bg pixel or the grid edge.
  80: 
  81:     Key insight: Rays emit only from the two endpoints of each outer-border segment, not every pixel, and travel diagonally away from the diamond.
  82:     """
